/* book exam traps: Using the physical length where the formula needs Leff. An 80 km span at 0.2 dB/km acts like 21.2 km. | Converting dB/km to nepers per metre wrongly. Divide by 4.343 for Np/km, and by 4343 for Np/m. | Swapping the two: Brillouin is backward, about 11 GHz, a band of tens of MHz; Raman is about 13 THz, a band of tens of THz. | Converting Aeff wrongly: 80 µm² is 80 × 10⁻¹² m², not 80 × 10⁻⁶ m². | Saying SRS limits each channel separately. Its wide band couples all channels, so it limits the total power. */
